Unless a file or directory contains a different explicit license notice, the material in this repository is source-available but is not open-source or open-data content. No copyright license is granted beyond the permissions stated below, the permissions required to operate the hosted Metkagram website, rights granted by the GitHub Terms of Service for public repositories, and rights that applicable law gives you independently of this notice.

2. What you may do without separate permission

You may:

- view the public repository and use the hosted Metkagram website as an end user;
- link to Metkagram pages and public records;
- cite Metkagram in research, teaching, commentary, or reviews;
- make limited quotations or other uses where applicable law permits them without a license.

These permissions do not include a right to copy or redistribute substantial parts of the corpus, source code, annotation system, datasets, schemas, translations, pattern collections, research materials, or visual assets.

3. Permission is required

Except where applicable law expressly permits the use, prior written permission is required to:

- copy, mirror, scrape, republish, or redistribute substantial portions of the repository or hosted datasets;
- modify or distribute the Metkagram source code or create a substantially derived implementation from it;
- create or redistribute derived corpora, pattern libraries, annotation datasets, or competing training collections based on substantial Metkagram material;
- use substantial Metkagram material to train or fine-tune models, build production retrieval corpora, or create commercial evaluation datasets;
- integrate the corpus, API exports, annotation scheme, or pattern collections into a commercial product or paid service;
- remove or obscure Metkagram provenance, attribution, canonical links, or rights notices.

4. Research and commercial licensing

Metkagram is open to research collaborations, supervised academic projects, institutional evaluation, language-data partnerships, API/data licensing, and commercial licensing. Permission can be scoped to a specific dataset, experiment, publication, integration, or period.

Start with the licensing page at https://metkagram.github.io/en/licensing/ or contact Metkagram through https://www.linkedin.com/company/metalhatscats.

5. Method and research identity

This notice protects copyrightable expression and other rights that may apply to Metkagram's code, documentation, corpus selection and arrangement, annotation materials, datasets, schemas, examples, translations, visual assets, and other concrete works. It does not claim copyright ownership over abstract ideas, general linguistic concepts, facts, or methods that copyright law does not protect.

